Active writes can block bucket ACL and property changes
Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/security/findings/44ce229d8c94819195ef00244e39043c?repo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fjustincormack%2Fargmin&sev=
Criticality: medium (attack path: medium)
Status: fixed

# Resolution
Fixed in commit `4c2768d` (`Exclude bucket runtime state from metadata commands`).

The fix projects `BucketRecord` down to command-owned bucket metadata at the
metadata-command boundary. Local runtime fields
`write_reservations_blocked`, `active_write_reservations`, and
`completed_multipart_upload_sequence` are no longer included in bucket command
checksums, retry matching, or PgStore bucket-command preimage equality. Bucket
command apply still preserves those local runtime fields on each replica.

Regression coverage was added for ACL, versioning, and public-access-block
commands while the routed bucket primary has an active local write reservation,
plus command-encoding coverage proving local runtime state is not serialized
into bucket command payloads.

Verification before the fix commit:
- `cargo nextest run -p storage`
- `cargo nextest run`
- `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`
- `cargo fmt`

